World Model: Chosen Next Action (from decision tree node)
- node_id: deep_pipeline
- base_node_id: root
- title: Deep pipeline with increased stream count and buffer depth
- difficulty_1_to_5: 2
- description: Increase CUDA streams from 2 to 8 and ring buffer depth from 8 to 32. Use larger transfer sizes (4 MiB). Ensure all SPDK completions immediately trigger H2D on the next available stream. This maximizes PCIe utilization by keeping multiple H2D transfers in flight and overlapping with NVMe reads.
- expected_vs_baseline_factor: 2.50x
- rationale: Current 2 streams with 8 buffers severely limits overlap. At 4 MiB per transfer and 16.8 GB/s PCIe, each H2D takes ~0.24ms. With only 2 in flight, we waste time on pipeline bubbles. 8 streams with 32 buffers allows full NVMe-to-PCIe overlap.

